---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/legal.css';
---
<Layout title="Terms of service | Bunco Score Keeper" showLegalLinks>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="description" content="The terms for using Bunco Score Keeper at bunco.io." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://bunco.io/terms.html" />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="page legal">
    <h1>Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated November 19, 2026</p>

    <p>These terms are an agreement between you and Brandon Meyer ("we"), who runs Bunco Score Keeper at bunco.io. By using the site, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.</p>

    <section class="index-card legal-summary" aria-labelledby="terms-summary">
      <h2 id="terms-summary">The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The site is free to use for your game nights.</li>
        <li>Anyone with your game code can join or change the game.</li>
        <li>The site only keeps score. It never takes or pays out money.</li>
        <li>We provide the site as it is, and games may not be saved forever.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">Using the site</h2>
    <p>There's no account to create and nothing to pay.</p>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">Your games</h2>
    <p>You're responsible for what you enter, including the names of other players. Use a first name or nickname, and don't enter anything private. Our <a href="privacy.html">privacy policy</a> explains who can see game information.</p>
    <p>Game codes are short and aren't passwords. Anyone who has one can join that game or change its scores.</p>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">Playing fair with the site</h2>
    <p>Please don't:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Change, disrupt, or delete games that aren't yours.</li>
      <li>Enter content that is unlawful, hateful, or harassing.</li>
      <li>Collect other people's information from the site.</li>
      <li>Overload the site, break its security, or interfere with how it runs.</li>
      <li>Use the site to break the law.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">Scores only, no money</h2>
    <p>Bunco Score Keeper only keeps score. It doesn't take payments, hold money, award prizes, or pay out anything based on how a game ends, and it isn't meant for betting. Any prize or bet is arranged by the people playing, not by us, and we aren't responsible for it. Your group settles any disagreement about scores.</p>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">Feedback</h2>
    <p>If you send us an idea or suggestion, we may use it without paying you or owing you anything.</p>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">Our content</h2>
    <p>The game of Bunco belongs to everyone. The site's design, text, and code belong to us, and you may not copy or resell them without permission.</p>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">Changes and availability</h2>
    <p>We may change, pause, or shut down any part of the site at any time. We may also remove games or other information. If a result matters to you, keep your own copy.</p>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">No warranties</h2>
    <p><strong>The site is provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied.</strong> This includes warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We don't promise that the site will be accurate, secure, uninterrupted, or free of errors.</p>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">Limit of liability</h2>
    <p><strong>To the fullest extent the law allows, we aren't liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost data, lost scores, disputes over results, or any prize or bet arranged outside the site. Our total liability for any claim about the site is limited to $50.</strong></p>
    <p>Some places don't allow these limits, so they may not all apply to you.</p>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>If these terms change, we'll post the new version here and update the date at the top. Continuing to use the site means you accept the new terms.</p>

    <h2 class="ruled-heading">Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? Email Brandon Meyer at <a href="mailto:privacy@bunco.io">privacy@bunco.io</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
